## Anti-Patterns (DO NOT)

❌ DO NOT use keyword matching ("diff" → always compare mode)
❌ DO NOT give shallow answers when detail is needed
❌ DO NOT skip agents that provide valuable perspective
❌ DO NOT skip agents to "save tokens" or "speed up" — cost is the user's call
❌ DO NOT forget customer perspective (Draupadi) — always check applicability
❌ DO NOT give only text - always include diagrams
❌ DO NOT assume - analyze the actual question
❌ DO NOT skip Krishna - every decision needs challenge
❌ DO NOT skip Money Lens - every decision has business impact
❌ DO NOT skip Decision Engine - always give final verdict
❌ DO NOT serialize independent agents — run Phase 3 trio and Phase 4 gates in PARALLEL
❌ DO NOT sequentialize Bhishma / Lakshman / Draupadi — always 3-way parallel
❌ DO NOT sequentialize Krishna / Money Lens — always 2-way parallel before Decision Engine
❌ DO NOT give wishy-washy conclusions - give clear GO / CONDITIONAL / NO-GO
❌ DO NOT trigger Emergency Override by inference — user must explicitly request it

## Must-Have in Every Response

1. **Real-world analogy** - Makes it understandable
2. **Visual diagram** - Shows the system
3. **Krishna's challenge** - What's wrong with this?
4. **Money perspective** - Business impact
5. **Clear verdict** - GO / CONDITIONAL / NO-GO
6. **Prioritized actions** - What to do next
